    "description": "holds canonicalizes relation then uses dot(offset,vec)>0 for vectors or forward reach before inverse reach for transitive relations. offset BFS subtracts signed adjacency vectors. path BFS retains first predecessor and reverses collected steps. Equations: pos[b]=(0,0); on first edge y→x carrying v set pos[x]=pos[y]−v. holds(a,r,b)=Some(pos[a]·vec(r)>0) when reachable. Transitive truth is reach_r(a,b), else false if reach_inverse(r)(a,b), else None.",
